OL,3,GNEWSAPrep begins before masts cut from
OL,4,Aexplosive wreck
OL,5,
OL,6,FPreparations are under way for the
OL,7,Fremoval of masts from an
OL,8,Fexplosives-filled World War Two ship in
OL,9,Fthe Thames Estuary.
OL,11,FVessels have been seen near the SS
OL,12,FRichard Montgomery wreck site, which
OL,13,Fhas been visible from Kent and Essex
OL,14,Fsince the US military vessel sank in
OL,15,F1944.
OL,17,FThe Department for Transport previously
OL,18,Fconfirmed work would start in September
OL,19,Fto remove the masts in case they fell
OL,20,Fon to and detonated 1,400 tonnes of
OL,21,Fexplosives that remain within the ship.
OL,23,APub: 16-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,323,320,200,140,0,100
